WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.540
Once an axon is chosen, how does cargo know which branch to go into?

2
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.770
Microtubules link choosing the axon to holding it.

3
00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.950
A microtubule has a fast-growing plus end and a slower minus end.

4
00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:19.923
Motor proteins read that direction.

5
00:00:20.883 --> 00:00:22.663
Most kinesins walk toward plus ends.

6
00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.083
Dynein walks toward minus ends.

7
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:27.703
Picture a plus-end-out track.

8
00:00:28.623 --> 00:00:30.663
Its plus end points away from the cell body.

9
00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:34.007
On that track, kinesin walks outward.

10
00:00:35.047 --> 00:00:36.947
Dynein walks home, toward the cell body.

11
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.420
On a minus-end-out track, it is the reverse.

12
00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:43.893
So which way do the tracks point in a real neuron?

13
00:00:44.983 --> 00:00:50.983
In 1988, Peter Baas and colleagues used hook decoration on cultured rat hippocampal

14
00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:51.983
neurons.

15
00:00:52.923 --> 00:00:56.243
Extra tubulin adds curved sheets to each microtubule's wall.

16
00:00:57.103 --> 00:00:59.803
In cross section, the hooks curve one way or the other.

17
00:01:00.833 --> 00:01:03.533
The curve shows which way that microtubule points.

18
00:01:04.566 --> 00:01:09.546
In the axon, nearly all microtubules point their plus ends away from the cell body.

19
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:13.070
In dendrites the orientation is mixed.

20
00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:15.490
A large fraction point each way.

21
00:01:16.433 --> 00:01:21.253
So which motor can carry cargo outward into a dendrite, but hardly ever into the

22
00:01:21.253 --> 00:01:22.253
axon?

23
00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:32.993
Dynein. It can carry cargo outward only on minus-end-out tracks.

24
00:01:34.083 --> 00:01:36.603
Vertebrate dendrites have many of those tracks.

25
00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:38.803
The axon has almost none.

26
00:01:39.783 --> 00:01:43.783
Kinesin can walk outward in both, since both have plus-end-out tracks.

27
00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:49.873
But a kinesin that prefers stable, plus-end-out microtubules can be steered into the

28
00:01:49.873 --> 00:01:50.873
axon.

29
00:01:51.366 --> 00:01:55.806
So the way the tracks point limits which motors can carry cargo outward into a

30
00:01:55.806 --> 00:01:56.806
process.

31
00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:59.196
That gives the neuron a sorting rule.

32
00:02:00.199 --> 00:02:03.979
The uniform plus-end-out array may form as the axon forms.

33
00:02:04.999 --> 00:02:08.819
If so, the tracks may help choose the axon, as well as keep it.

34
00:02:10.049 --> 00:02:14.089
Flies differ. Their dendrites are mostly minus-end-out.

35
00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:17.133
So the details depend on the animal.

36
00:02:17.993 --> 00:02:20.773
But in both, axon and dendrites offer different tracks.

37
00:02:21.816 --> 00:02:24.376
Different tracks, different motors, different cargo.

38
00:02:25.276 --> 00:02:26.696
The tracks may be part of the hold.

39
00:02:27.776 --> 00:02:29.556
Next, the gate at the start of the axon.
